Make pillow's setup.py build against the cross target instead of the build
host. This file is for pillow 12.x and later and is the one current builds
use; setup-10.x.patch covers the older line, and meta.yaml picks between them
by version. The split exists because 12.x dropped `self.add_imaging_libs = ""`
from `initialize_options`, leaving the older file's first hunk without
matching context. 12.x also carries upstream's own iOS support
(`get_ios_sdk_path` plus a `sys.platform == "ios"` branch), so the Apple SDK
backport that makes up most of the older file has nothing to do here, while
points 2 to 4 below have no counterpart there.

pillow does not ask the compiler what it can reach. Its `pil_build_ext`
collects candidate include and library directories itself, probes them for
zlib.h, libjpeg, libfreetype and the rest, and compiles in whatever it
believes it found. Every one of those probes runs on the build machine, so
left alone a cross-build measures the macOS or Linux runner and bakes the
answer into an iOS or Android wheel.

  1. `disable_platform_guessing` is forced True instead of being read from
     setup.cfg. It is the master switch for the "add platform directories"
     chain and the "standard locations" block after it: /sw, X11 and the
     macOS SDK on darwin, ldconfig output on linux, and /usr/local/{lib,
     include}, /usr/{lib,include} and /lib everywhere. With it on, nothing
     pillow might stumble over on the runner (libtiff, OpenJPEG, libwebp,
     lcms2, libimagequant) can switch itself on, and the recipe's host deps
     become exactly the wheel's feature set.

     The same switch also drops the branch that would add the target SDK's
     usr/include and usr/lib. iOS is unaffected, because Python-Apple-
     support's sysconfig already puts the SDK include path on
     `compiler.include_dirs`; the Android cross-venv surfaces nothing
     comparable, its NDK paths living in CFLAGS and LDFLAGS, which distutils
     never reflects into the directory lists. Replacing them is what the
     CPATH and LIBRARY_PATH entries in meta.yaml are for, and the comment
     there has the detail.

     The hunk also sets `disable_brotli`, for which see its inline comment.
     Worth knowing before relying on it: "brotli" is not one of the names in
     `ext_feature.features`, so nothing in 12.x reads the attribute and the
     assignment is a guard against a future in which it becomes a real
     feature. What keeps brotli off the link line today is point 4.

  2. `sys.prefix/lib` and `sys.prefix/include` are added unconditionally by
     upstream, ahead of every guessing check, so point 1 does not stop them.
     Under crossenv that prefix is the build-side venv, whose headers belong
     to the build interpreter; gating the two calls on platform guessing
     leaves the target with its own.

  3. Host paths that leak in through the compiler object are filtered out.
     They arrive not from pillow's own lists but from the build Python's
     sysconfig, which is why point 1 cannot remove them, and the filter has
     to sit immediately after pillow prepends its directories to
     `self.compiler.{include,library}_dirs` and before the feature probing
     that reads those same lists. The match is against exact paths rather
     than `d.startswith("/usr/")` for the reason spelled out in the comment
     inside the hunk: pillow realpath()s every directory it collects, GitHub
     runners keep $ANDROID_HOME under /usr/local/lib/android/sdk, and a
     prefix test would therefore strip the NDK sysroot that CPATH exists to
     supply, taking zlib detection with it.

  4. The iOS transitive-link list for `_imagingft` drops to z and bz2.
     Upstream, new in 12.0, also links brotlicommon, brotlidec and png, which
     suits a freetype built the way Apple's is; flet-libfreetype is built
     without brotli and libpng, no such archives are staged, and the link
     fails with `ld: library 'brotlicommon' not found`. z and bz2 stay
     because freetype references them without linking them into its static
     archive.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -372,11 +372,17 @@
         return True if value in configuration.get(option, []) else None

     def initialize_options(self) -> None:
-        self.disable_platform_guessing = self.check_configuration(
-            "platform-guessing", "disable"
-        )
+        self.disable_platform_guessing = True
         build_ext.initialize_options(self)
         for x in self.feature:
             setattr(self, f"disable_{x}", self.check_configuration(x, "disable"))
             setattr(self, f"enable_{x}", self.check_configuration(x, "enable"))
+        # Mobile-forge: force-disable optional features whose libraries
+        # mobile-forge does NOT supply via host deps. Pillow 12 added
+        # brotli to the link line whenever the headers can be reached;
+        # on iOS the cross site-packages happens to expose them, so the
+        # build pulls in `-lbrotlicommon -lbrotlidec` but no matching
+        # static archive exists in the link search path, breaking the
+        # _imaging.so link with `ld: library 'brotlicommon' not found`.
+        self.disable_brotli = True
         for x in ("raqm", "fribidi"):
@@ -547,8 +545,10 @@
                 for d in os.environ[k].split(os.path.pathsep):
                     _add_directory(library_dirs, d)
 
-        _add_directory(library_dirs, os.path.join(sys.prefix, "lib"))
-        _add_directory(include_dirs, os.path.join(sys.prefix, "include"))
+        # Skip sys.prefix paths when cross-compiling to avoid host headers
+        if not self.disable_platform_guessing:
+            _add_directory(library_dirs, os.path.join(sys.prefix, "lib"))
+            _add_directory(include_dirs, os.path.join(sys.prefix, "include"))
 
         #
         # add platform directories
@@ -683,6 +683,31 @@
         self.compiler.include_dirs = include_dirs + self.compiler.include_dirs
 
         #
+        # When cross-compiling, drop the host's Linux system include/lib
+        # paths that leak in from the build Python's sysconfig (e.g. a
+        # system-installed CPython contributing /usr/include).
+        #
+        # Match exact paths only — NOT `d.startswith("/usr/")` — because
+        # pillow's `_add_directory` calls `os.path.realpath()`, so a
+        # CPATH entry pointing inside the Android NDK resolves through
+        # whatever symlink chain the runner uses. On GitHub Actions
+        # `$ANDROID_HOME=/usr/local/lib/android/sdk`, so the NDK
+        # sysroot include path realpaths to
+        # `/usr/local/lib/android/sdk/ndk/<ver>/.../sysroot/usr/include`
+        # — `startswith("/usr/")` matches that and the prefix-based
+        # filter ends up stripping the very headers CPATH was set to
+        # surface for zlib detection.
+        if self.disable_platform_guessing:
+            _host_leaks = frozenset({
+                "/usr/include", "/usr/local/include",
+                "/usr/lib", "/usr/local/lib",
+                # Debian/Ubuntu multi-arch:
+                "/usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu",
+                "/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu",
+            })
+            self.compiler.include_dirs = [d for d in self.compiler.include_dirs if d not in _host_leaks]
+            self.compiler.library_dirs = [d for d in self.compiler.library_dirs if d not in _host_leaks]
+        #
         # look for available libraries

         feature = self.feature
@@ -998,7 +1023,7 @@

             if sys.platform == "ios":
                 # Ensure transitive dependencies are linked.
-                libs.extend(["z", "bz2", "brotlicommon", "brotlidec", "png"])
+                libs.extend(["z", "bz2"])

             self._update_extension("PIL._imagingft", libs, defs, srcs)
